# business-game

C++23 SFML 2D skeleton: `Game` runs against `WindowI` (SFML adapter on the executable), plus a windowless `Example` type in `gameLib`. Longer-term notes live in `mvp/` (`01`–`09` prospect, `10` living); do not assume menu, Arkanoid, screens, or a board-game exist in the code.

## Stack

- C++23, CMake ≥ 3.20, Ninja presets (`debug` / `release`)
- SFML 3.1 via FetchContent (`cmake/FetchSFML.cmake`) — Graphics/Window/System only; no manual SFML install
- GoogleTest 1.18 only in Debug; clang-format / clang-tidy at repo root

## Layout

- `src/main.cpp` — `WindowSFML` + `Game{window}.run()`
- `src/Game.hpp` / `Game.cpp` — process loop; `WindowI&` only (`gameLib`)
- `src/window/` — `WindowI`, `WindowSFML` (`WindowSFML.cpp` on executable `game`)
- `src/Example.hpp` / `Example.cpp` — `gameLib`
- `tests/unit_tests/` — `example_test`, `game_test`
- `tests/mocks/window/WindowMock.hpp`

Static library target: `gameLib`. Executable: `game`.

## Build / test

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target game
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

Binary: `build/<preset>/bin/game` (`.exe` on Windows).

## Agent pitfalls

- New `.cpp` files that belong in the library must be listed in `src/CMakeLists.txt` (`gameLib`)
- `WindowSFML.cpp` is listed on the `game` executable, not in `gameLib`
- `gameLib` does not **link** SFML (headers/defines only); the `game` executable links Graphics/Window/System
- Interfaces use the `FooI` suffix (`WindowI`); later mvp names such as `IScreen` become `ScreenI` when they land
- Design notes: `mvp/01`–`09` (prospect). Tree names and slices: `mvp/10-engine-progress.md`
